OnePlus 15 @RELEASE_TAG@ boot-only TWRP installer
=================================================

This archive is a boot-only installer for:

  OnePlus 15 / infiniti / canoe
  @FIRMWARE@
  kernel release: @KERNEL_RELEASE@
  source commit: @SOURCE_COMMIT@

A release tag containing "candidate" or "test" identifies an unqualified
physical-test package. It must not be represented as stable or physically
qualified until this exact ZIP has passed the repository's device gates.

Archive contents
----------------

  boot.img
    bytes: @BOOT_BYTES@
    sha256: @BOOT_SHA256@

  kernel-info.txt
  checksums.sha256
  META-INF/com/google/android/update-binary
  META-INF/com/google/android/updater-script

It intentionally does not contain a custom system_dlkm image.

Required installed firmware contract
------------------------------------

The active slot must already use the untouched stock @FIRMWARE@
system_dlkm EROFS image:

  bytes checked: @STOCK_SYSTEM_DLKM_BYTES@
  EROFS magic at offset 1024: @STOCK_SYSTEM_DLKM_EROFS_MAGIC@
  sha256: @STOCK_SYSTEM_DLKM_SHA256@

The installer positively verifies the infiniti/canoe OnePlus 15 family, the
active A/B slot, exact firmware version, EROFS magic, and stock DLKM hash before any
write. It refuses an active OTA snapshot/merge, ext4 system_dlkm, a modified
system_dlkm, an unknown firmware, or a device that cannot be verified.

Installer-supported family identifiers: CPH2745 / CPH2747 / CPH2749 / PLK110.
The marketing model (including "OnePlus 15"), regional code and software
fingerprint are diagnostic information, not hardware authentication.
Explicit infiniti identity and canoe evidence are required. Audited stock/
TWRP OP611FL1 and OP60FFL1 device aliases additionally require project 24831
or 24863 if no infiniti property is exposed. Generic SM8850 is insufficient.

Physically qualified kernel: CPH2747 only, with the coverage in its validation
report. Other regional variants: SUPPORTED BY DEVICE FAMILY DETECTION --
PHYSICAL REPORTS REQUESTED. The corrected installer ZIP itself has not yet
been physically tested. Family detection does not prove a different regional
module stack compatible. A different stock DLKM hash still fails closed;
do not cross-flash DLKM or regional firmware to get past this guard.

What it does
------------

* Extracts and SHA-256 verifies boot.img.
* Resolves distinct boot_a and boot_b nodes, then selects the active slot.
* Measures actual boot capacity before any write. This full-partition AVB
  image requires capacity exactly equal to @BOOT_BYTES@ bytes; smaller targets
  fail the capacity check, larger targets need a separately validated container.
* Creates a complete durable backup of boot_<active-slot> and requires its
  SHA-256 to equal the source partition hash before writing.
* Flashes only boot_<active-slot>.
* Reads back the complete boot partition and verifies the exact boot SHA-256.
* Restores the boot backup if writing or read-back verification fails.

What it never does
------------------

* It never writes, mounts, maps, unmaps, resizes, erases, or otherwise changes
  system_dlkm or system_dlkm_oki.
* It never writes vendor_boot, vendor_dlkm, dtbo, vbmeta, vbmeta_system, or
  vbmeta_vendor.
* Regional modem/radio/persist partitions, userdata and metadata are untouched.
* It does not modify dynamic-partition metadata or disable AVB verification.

Requirements
------------

* An unlocked OnePlus 15 on the exact firmware above.
* TWRP, OrangeFox or PBRP with the required lpdump and Android recovery tools.
  Missing optional properties are tolerated; missing positive family/platform,
  active-slot, snapshot, backup or firmware evidence is not bypassed.
* Decrypted /data or durable mounted external storage for the boot backup.

Install the ZIP from TWRP, then reboot System without switching slots. This is
firmware-specific: do not install it on any other OxygenOS build.

The generated system_dlkm.flatten.ext4.img remains a development and recovery
fallback artifact. It is not part of this boot-only installer.
